    <static seed="18" source="Library/ASU-topics/setLogarithmicFunctions/srw4_5_5.pg">
      <statement><p>The population of a certain city was 299000 in 2018, and the observed relative
growth rate is 2 percent per year.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>Let <m>t</m> be the number of years after 2018 and <m>r</m> be the relative growth rate.  Find a function that models the population after <m>t</m> years.</p>
<p><m>P(t)=</m> <fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Find the projected population in the year 2027: <fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>In what year will the population reach 418672? <fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>299000\cdot 1.02^{t}</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>357333</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>2035</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <solution><p>a. The model will be an exponential model: <m>P(t) =  a(1+r)^t</m>, where the initial population will be <m>a=229000</m> and growth rate as <m>r=2/100 = 0.02</m>.  The model then is</p>
<p><me>P(t) = 299000\ast1.02^t</me></p>
<p>b. To find the projected population, first note that 2027 is <m>t=9</m> years after 2018. This value of <m>t</m> will be substituted into the model so</p>
<p><me>P(9) = 299000\ast1.02^{9} = {357333}</me></p>
<p>c. Use logarithms to solve the equation 
<m>\displaystyle{{418672}=299000\ast 1.02^t }</m> for <m>t</m>.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}
        {418672}\amp =299000\ast 1.02^t \\
        {418672}/299000 \amp = 1.02^t \\
        {1.40024} \amp = 1.02^t \\
        \ln({1.40024}) \amp = \ln\big(1.02^t\big)=t \ln(1.02) \\
        t \amp = \frac{\ln({1.40024})}{\ln(1.02)}\\
        t \amp = {17} \end{aligned}}</m></p>
<p>So the year is <m>2018+t =2035</m></p>
</solution>
